gametitle=Grrrand Theft Auto!: San Andreas (PAL-M5) (v1.03) SLES-52541 A1A3F231 | A1B3F232

TITLE:		GTA SAN_ANDREAS CHEATS
AUTHOR:	TKBS
DATE:		2025, Updated 2026.
GAME: 		GTA SAN_ANDREAS PAL Black (Version 1 (v1.03)) 2004 SLES-52541
CRC:		A1B3F232 = (PALv1-50hz) - Original
CRC:		A1A3F231 = (PALv1-60hz) - Patched .elf
CREDITS	TKBS
CREDITS	Respective Authors.
Links: 		OrionSR post:	https://gtaforums.com/topic/350108-cheat-code-creation/
Links:  		info on pnach: 	https://slymods.info/wiki/Guide:Writing_pnach_files | https://slymods.info/wiki/Guide:Writing_pnach_files#Increment_/_Decrement

File Number 1/3 * See Files 2/3 & 3/3 for more

Before You Begin;-
	Users should test the game as default, then try this file, then create their own file using the resources provided.
			There are 3 Pnach files. They should be organised as follows;-
				File Number 1/3 the file author uses
								codes already enabled, based on personal preference, some unique stuff.
								an attempt to put things in alphabetical order is made
				File Number 2/3	Should contain everything
								organised with " ---- A ---- " --> " ---- Z ---- " headers
								all codes should be tested and with notes.
				File Number 3/3	contains all junk notes and crap (source) from research etc.
								may contain useful information, but mostly crap.
								contains all unsolved stuff or things that work in one version but not another.
								also some random and unique stuff that remains unfinished.
				Optional:
						Due to the large amount of patches possible;-
						a) the STATS should have a dedicated file {STAT, Address}, but i was unable to catelog them all.
						b) there are 2 methods to activate/ deactivate the 91 cheats, pick 1 method to keep the file smaller, save the other to another file.
						note: use the link for the PC list, retain ordering, add PS2 adddresses and note any differences.
						* it would be very beneficial to ensure all 91 cheats are listed correctly and all STATS, this will show the BLANK memory regions which will be useful.

IMPORTANT	* ".pnach" patches here created for PCSX2 1.6.0. - The effects of patches (for any game) differ depending on BIOS, PCSX2 Version.
			* Use the "GTSA-Cheats_Companion_App.exe" with this ".pnach"

----------------------------
---- New Inputs;- ----
----------------------------
* Cheats & Debug options have been created similar to vice city hybrid ("VCH") version.

"Main.scm (Modified)"
			Show Coordinates 				Runs all the time & Includes "Spawn Explosions".
			PAD 2 - {SELECT, START}		Skip Missions**
			PAD 1 - {SELECT + X}			OPEN Cheat menu 1 (Cheats)
			PAD 1 - {SELECT + L1}		OPEN Cheat menu 2 (Teleport Destinations)
			PAD 1 - {SELECT + R1}		OPEN Cheat menu 3 (Teleport oddjobs)
			-------Removed	------->		Open Cheat Menu 4 (Weather Menu) - Removed, set weather with ".pnach" instead.
			PAD 1 - {SELECT + SQUARE}	CLOSE
			PAD 1 - {CIRCLE}				Vehicles: "Spawn Explosions" a few feet in front you (When in Vehicles)
											This is embedded in the show coordinates script, which users can disable entirely using pnach.
											206B0774 (0,1)

".pnach"
			PAD 1 - {SQUARE }			Dynamic Jump: TAP = super jump | Hold = control gravity
			PAD 1 - {DOWN + START}		Open Save Menu - Save (or pause) anywhere - Do Not Save During Missions!
			PAD 1 - {L1 + R1}				Vehicles: Lock & Unlock Vehicle Doors (Hold = locked, release = unlock)
			PAD 1 - {R2 + LEFT}			Vehicles: Vortex Fix (Work-around)
			PAD 1 - {R1 + R2}				MAGIC_CAR - Vehicles: Spawn Vehicle Enabler
			PAD 1 - {L1 + L2}				MAGIC_CAR - Vehicles: Spawn Vehicle Disabler (Reset)
			PAD 1 - {R1 }					MAGIC_CAR - Vehicles: Increment Vehicle ID +1, ensuring write access for cheat companion app.
			PAD 1 - {SELECT + LEFT}		Weapons (1)

".exe" (Companion app);-

			Decrement/ Increment	Vehicle ID					L2 / R2 or Numerics (+)/(-)
			Numerics (0-9) to toggle CHEATS
			Use Numpad to enter coordinates (x,y,z) for teleport (Use Numpad to avoid conflict with numerics.)
			Type vehicle model name, or number,  from "vehicles.ide" or name from "american.gxt".

**DO NOT SKIP;-
	- important phone calls.
	- maddog jump out of plane 'parachute' mission. wait until you jump out the plane.
	- the "end of the line". causes end cutscenes to not play.
	- there is no vigilante skip. Rockstar did not add it and i could not get it working. Use .pnach instead to auto-complete or drive around using "Spawn Explosions".

----------------------------
Features;-
----------------------------
		These Features are included;-
			Teleport anywhere
			Spawn any Vehicle
			Music Outside Vehicle
			Modify game Attributes and Render options
			Dynamic Brightness HUD, Radar, Jump, Punch examples.
			Cheat companion App
			PAL support
			Fixes
			FOV++

----------------------------
Fixes:
----------------------------
		These Fixes are included;-
			1. See - skimmer (vehicles.ide) & "Vortex Pay and Spray Fix" by TKBS
			2. See - GXT typos
			3. See - fixing where others may have gone wrong.

----------------------------
Mods;-
----------------------------
		These Mods are included;-
			Main.scm 		- fix and add cheat menus.
			.ELF 			- patch 60hz
			occlusion Files 	- set to 0's
			peds.Coll 		- fix loading in editor
			vehicles.ide 	- fix skimmer
			fileload 			- remove 2nd img dependency

----------------------------
Notes;-
----------------------------
			There are multiple variants for patches. The exact, or best method per-patch is debatable.

----------------------------
OFFSETS
----------------------------
			To Convert PAL to NTSC (v1 = +100) || (NTSC v2 = A90) aprrox. Sometimes they are same address with different values, or instructions.

----------------------------
Recommendations;-
----------------------------
			1. Use Save files to transfer pnach changes easily from PC to Console.
				- Codebreaker.bin file USB method - NOT TESTED.
			2. Use NotePad++ ".xml" for colourful ".pnach" Language styling.
			3. Use "GTSA-Cheats(pnach_companion_app).exe" with pcsx2.exe 1.6.0.
			4. Use ".ct" file with cheat engine.

----------------------------
Known Issues;-
----------------------------
			1. Codebreaker: some codes might not work when converted.
			2. Patches not working:  Save State & Reload Emulator.
			3. Not compatible with pcsx2 1.7+, q-t, etc.
			4. Extended functions
				- It is possible a later version of pcsx2 may work with more extended functions
				- i still don't understand this E##### Stuff. My examples are based on what i tested and work, but other examples online are different.
				- example - compare slymods info vs OrionSR's info vs Mine, vs the actual results - as shown below you cannot do both. i.e. if we use a 1 or 2 for less than or equal, we cannot also execute multiple line and they can't both be right for different functions.

----------------------------
Unsolved;-
----------------------------
			1. ON_MISSION flag address needed 	- would allow for much better patches.
			2. IN_VEHICLE flag address needed 		- would allow for much better patches.
			3. TELEPORT to properties with auto-purchase function - see Vice City Hybrid Cheats & Debug patches.
			4. CINEMATIC flag address needed (where HUD dissappears and CJ switches to self controlled view mode.)
			5. Red Marker coordinates address from menu map.
			6. and many more...

----------------------------
Not Tested;-
----------------------------
			1. Hardware: PS2 + Keyboard / or PS3, & the native .scm ps2_kb functions.
			2. Software: GSM or with YPOS patch on official hardware.
			3. Software: codebreaker save file with YPOS
			4. Hardware: PS4

