		- something writes to widescreen address preventing it from being modified. (4:3 1.33 | 16:9 1.777) --> 1:888 (720x576)
3. 	a fix for the FOV when flying at high altitude and high speed.
4.  all stats memory regions, so that we know which are blank memory regions.
5. 	port dynamic brightness to cheat companion app.

----------------------------
Emulator;-
----------------------------
	PCSX2 Q-T: DO NOT use QT, or any version above 1.6.0, but if you do, then do this...
		* The "GameIndex.yaml" Contains shit we want to remove: 	"C:\Games\PS2\Emulator\PCSX2-qt\resources"
		... * & has patches files here: 									"C:\Games\PS2\Emulator\PCSX2-qt\resources\patches.zip"
		* remove patches because they are out-dated, not labelled or documented & interfere with patches creation.
		* then use this file to re-make patches for the latest pcsx2 version.

	These settings are baked in - REMOVE THEM and use this pnach instead!
		SLES-52541:
		name: "Grand Theft Auto - San Andreas"
		region: "PAL-M5"
		compat: 5
		clampModes:
		eeClampMode: 2 # Fixes Game freezes during "Reuniting The Families" mission.
		gsHWFixes:
		recommendedBlendingLevel: 2 # Fixes blocky heat haze effect.
		halfPixelOffset: 5 # Helps align radiosity closer to native.
		autoFlush: 1 # Fixes post-processing.
	* None of the above settings were needed in pcsx2 1.6.0 - and i completed game without cheats and no issues occured.
	* the gameindex.dbf doesn't do anythign in cpsx2 1.6.0 either.
	* pcsx2 2.6.3 (latest) has noticable visual quality loss, integrated stuff that is not documented and interferes with other stuff, and is generally just a horrible experience to use.
	* it does not offer any advantages over pcsx2 1.6.0, infact it makes things worse for gta, which is why they integrate stuff without telling the users and why people have to make patches to fix patches.
	* the simple fact that the important info required for the end user is not present, like all current day stuff, highlights how little they give a shit.

